From 4d99bb7c39ec505c0210c3408917af256eee66e2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 05:24:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fly: no held buttons -- A taps a 0.5 s climb pulse, LT
 toggles descent

Hard rule (CLAUDE.md: no held-button gameplay); settled SYSTEMS Fly spec and
the #356 interim descent ruling. fly_controller.gd read `jump` and
`fly_descend` as held states (climb in a current while A was held; descend
while LT was held).

- A fresh A tap starts a 0.5 s pulse climbing AT 8 m/s and paying climb
  stamina (1.6/s); another fresh tap refreshes the remainder to 0.5 s, never
  stacks; holding A repeats nothing (edges only). The launch press is not
  also a climb tap.
- Inside a valid authored updraft the tap rides the current up to its
  ceiling: a tap-started channel that continues while the flyer stays in it,
  so authored updraft behaviour is preserved without holding; reaching the
  roof stops the rise there.
- `fly_descend` is a tap toggle: descend until landing or the next tap; a
  climb tap also ends it; landing clears it.
- Numbers in data/config/fly_traversal.json (climb_pulse_seconds 0.5,
  climb_pulse_mps 8.0).
- Route harnesses (smoke_cloudreach_continuous, helpers/cloudreach_live_segment)
  tap toward the flight state they want via `_fly_intent` instead of holding.

Tests: test_cloudreach_fly_no_hold.gd (config, pulse, refresh, no repeat,
input-owned, current ride, descend toggle, mutual cancel, no held reads);
smoke_cloudreach_fly_no_hold.gd (real input on the production Player).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01AbnCQbYpP3f5KQ9hTrct95
